      "blockers": [],
      "notes": [
        "Every projection exposes hand_n while ordinary opponents receive no hidden identities or hidden-zone movement names. Owners retain complete hand access outside their priority window and while controlling another player; CR 723.4 adds the controlled hand without replacing the controller's own. A directly observed public-to-hand transition remains in known_hand but does not grant full hand inspection. A targeted public reveal makes every current hand identity known to all live seats, while a look makes those identities known only to the resolving controller; exact replay preserves both knowledge states. Hand ordering is private and rules-insignificant."
      ]
